## 1. Ticket Types & Labels

**Canonical mechanism: GitHub Issue Types.** Issue Types are defined at the organization level (Settings → Planning → Issue types) and are unavailable on user-owned repositories such as this one today (`repository.issueTypes` is `null`). If the repo is transferred to an organization, define one Issue Type per row below (same names), set the type on every open issue, and the Type *labels* in this table are retired (the rows stay as the definition of each type).

**Fallback while the repo is user-owned:** every issue created MUST apply exactly one primary **Type** label from this standard taxonomy:

| Type Label | Color | Ticket Type | Purpose / Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `epic` | `3E4B9E` | **Epic** | Large body of work spanning multiple sprints/milestones, broken into smaller user stories or tasks. |
| `user-story` | `0052CC` | **User Story / Feature** | New user-facing capability or requirement written from the user's perspective with observable AC. |
| `bug` | `D73A4A` | **Bug / Defect** | Unexpected error or defect requiring troubleshooting and a fix. |
| `task` | `0E8A16` | **Task** | General non-user-facing technical work (e.g. environment config, CI/CD, docs update). |
| `sub-task` | `5319E7` | **Sub-task** | Granular, actionable piece broken off from a larger story or task. |
| `spike` | `BFD4F2` | **Spike / Research** | Time-boxed investigative research or prototyping to reduce technical uncertainty before building. |
| `tech debt` | `C2E0C6` | **Tech Debt / Refactor** | Code cleanup, refactoring, or maintainability improvement without changing external behavior. |

### Area labels

Add one or more `area:*` labels when the component area is known (all use color `1D76DB`). The taxonomy mirrors the module split of the firmware and the instrument subsystems:

| Area Label | Covers |
|---|---|
| `area:thermal` | Block and lid temperature control, PID, Peltier drive, calibration |
| `area:safety` | Sensor fault detection, overtemperature cutoff, heater verification, watchdog, safe state |
| `area:optics` | Excitation, detection, fluorescence reads, Ct calling, sample calls |
| `area:protocol` | Protocol model, step runner, loops, melt curves, presets |
| `area:ui` | Touchscreen screens, LEDs, buzzer |
| `area:comms` | App link, message protocol, WiFi/BLE, time sync, firmware update |
| `area:data` | Run records, raw data storage, logs, export |
| `area:platform` | Board-agnostic core, hardware interface, board targets, build system |
| `area:hardware` | Electronics, BOM, mechanical, block, enclosure |
| `area:testing` | Host unit tests, replay tests, bench validation, fault injection |
| `area:ci` | GitHub Actions, build pipeline, release automation |

If no `area:*` label fits, file the issue without one and propose a new row in this table via PR. Do not invent a one-off name.

