## 2. Priority Taxonomy & Labels

Every issue created MUST apply exactly one **Priority** label:

| Priority Label | Color | Priority Level | SLA / Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| `P0 - Emergency` | `000000` | **P0 (Emergency)** | Critical blocker / production outage — drop everything and fix immediately. |
| `P1 - High` | `B60205` | **P1 (High)** | High priority — planned for immediate next work. |
| `P2 - Medium` | `FBCA04` | **P2 (Medium)** | Standard backlog priority. |
| `P3 - Low` | `0E8A16` | **P3 (Low)** | Low priority / deferred work. |
| `P4 - Nice to Have` | `C5DEF5` | **P4 (Nice to Have)** | Optional improvement — no timeline commitment. |

### Verifying the label set

Before filing, confirm the labels you intend to use exist exactly as named:

```bash
gh label list --repo jeremiahlandi/Portable-qPCR-System --limit 100 --json name --jq '.[].name' | sort
```

If a taxonomy label is missing or its color/description has drifted from the tables above, stop and report it (or, with explicit user authorization, repair it with `gh label create` / `gh label edit` using the exact values from the table). Never work around a missing label by picking a different one.

