## 3. Required Ticket Structure (10-Section Template)

Every ticket body MUST follow this comprehensive structured template:

```markdown
## 1. Executive Summary & Goal
Brief high-level summary of what this ticket accomplishes and why.

## 2. User Story / Objective
As a [role], I want [goal], so that [value].

## 3. Background & Context
Relevant context, history, design links, or related issues. Parent: #<n> (informational — the native sub-issue link is the source of truth, see §0).

## 4. Scope & Non-Scope
- **In Scope:** Explicitly what will be built / investigated.
- **Out of Scope:** Explicitly what will NOT be done in this ticket.

## 5. Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Testable, observable condition
- [ ] Error state handling
- [ ] Empty / fallback state handling

## 6. Data & State Requirements
Inputs, schema fields, validation rules, persisted data, or API contracts.

## 7. Dependencies & Blockers
Prerequisite tickets, external assets, or technical dependencies (or "None").

## 8. Actionable Tasks
- [ ] Task step 1
- [ ] Task step 2

## 9. Assumptions & Decision References
- [ ] Assumption to confirm with user
Decision reference: LI-DL-### (or "none applies")

## 10. QA & Verification Protocol
Concrete steps for how to verify this work once completed.
```

---

## 4. Guardrails & Rules

- **Mandatory Hierarchy:** Never leave a non-epic issue without a native parent (§0). Filing is not complete until the sub-issue link is verified.
- **Mandatory Type & Priority:** Never create a ticket without exactly one **Type** (Issue Type where available; otherwise the label `epic`, `user-story`, `bug`, `task`, `sub-task`, `spike`, `tech debt`) and exactly one **Priority** label (`P0 - Emergency` … `P4 - Nice to Have`). A ticket missing either is non-compliant and must be fixed with `gh issue edit --add-label` before it is considered filed.
- **Closed Taxonomy:** Only labels defined in §1 and §2 may be applied or created. Any new label requires a change to this rule first.
- **Authorization Required:** Draft the full ticket body and present it to the user for sign-off before executing `gh issue create`.
- **No Guessed Intent:** Cite `LI-DL-###` decision references (this repo's decision log) when applicable. Never invent business intent. Decisions for this repo are numbered `LI-DL-###` in a shared sequence with the other Landi Industries repos; none have been recorded for this repo yet. Candidate decisions to record first: controller board, block sensor, GPL acceptance for ported Klipper code.
- **Platform Constraint:** NEVER create tickets on Linear, Jira, or any platform other than GitHub Issues.

